.TH BISYNC-SYNCED 1 "October 2026" "scripts" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bisync-synced \- bidirectional Google Drive synchronization with Btrfs snapshot protection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bisync-synced
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fB\-\-resync\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry-run\fR]
[\fB\-\-status\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBbisync-synced\fR executes a resilient bidirectional synchronization between a local directory
(default: \fB$HOME/Remote/Synced\fR) and a remote Google Drive destination (default: \fBgdrive_dev:Synced\fR)
using \fBrclone bisync\fR.
.PP
Before initiating data synchronization, if the target directory resides on a \fBBtrfs\fR subvolume, the script
automatically captures a timestamped, read-only Btrfs snapshot in \fB$HOME/.local/share/gdrive_snapshots\fR.
This provides instantaneous rollback protection against remote deletions or split-brain sync conflicts.
Snapshots are automatically pruned, retaining the 5 most recent snapshots.
.PP
Concurrent runs are prevented via non-blocking file locking (\fBflock\fR). Live progress and status are reported
via desktop notifications.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command synopsis and configurable environment variables.
.TP
.B \-\-resync
Forces a full resynchronization baseline pass (passed directly to \fBrclone bisync\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Executes a simulation run without creating snapshots or modifying remote/local files.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Displays lock state and the last 20 lines of the synchronization log.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SYNC_SUBVOL
Local synchronization path (default: \fB$HOME/Remote/Synced\fR).
.TP
.B SYNC_REMOTE
Rclone remote target (default: \fBgdrive_dev:Synced\fR).
.TP
.B SYNC_SNAP_DIR
Directory for local Btrfs snapshots (default: \fB$HOME/.local/share/gdrive_snapshots\fR).
.TP
.B SYNC_FILTER_FILE
Rclone filter definitions file (default: \fB$HOME/.config/rclone/bisync-synced.filter\fR).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rclone (1),
.BR btrfs (8),
.BR scripts (1)
